  "goodToKnow": "Der Marktplatz is the market square, the historic heart of most German towns, usually with the Rathaus (town hall), a fountain and a church nearby. Weekly markets (der Wochenmarkt) still take place there, and in December it hosts the Weihnachtsmarkt. Bremen's Marktplatz, with its Roland statue, is a UNESCO World Heritage site. Online, ein Marktplatz is a trading platform."
